From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:40:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] images: check deferred lazy images on scroll, behind a pref
 (T-558)

Upstream's lazy loading (the previous commit) polls each deferred image
on its own timer. On the TouchPad that is a timer per image on a long
page. The deferred images of a document now share one set, checked 50 ms
after a scroll event of any of the document's scroll frames (a drag's
events coalesce) and every 2 s as a safety net for layout that moves an
image into view without a scroll. An image leaves the set on every load
path, unbind and destruction. jihad.images.lazy (default false) gates it:
off, loading="lazy" is read as eager, as before, until the lever is
measured.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MpagfP34fXBdsc76E8YSzR
